review_comments.body:
Hmm...
We have two issues that we want to solve:

1. Respect a provided custom compiler
2. Compile the custom compiler providing the needed schemas and opts.

This kind of solves both, but I feel it is quite fragile following this path.

Did we consider something like...?
```js
  setupValidator (serverOptions) {
    // We seek if there's a custom compiler already added, no compiler at all
   // and no new schemas added.
    const isReady = !this.isCustomValidatorCompiler && this.validatorCompiler !== undefined && !this.addedSchemas
    if (isReady) {
      return
    }

		// We can shortcut checks to avoid this, but it might do the work already.
    this.validatorCompiler = this.isCustomValidatorCompiler && this.validatorCompiler != null ? this.validatorCompiler : this.getValidatorBuilder()(this.schemaBucket.getSchemas(), serverOptions.ajv)
  }
```

Is similar (or equal) to what @Eomm suggested in the first place.

do you foresee any issue with this approach @derammo?

